<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ludvík Svoboda</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1895–1979</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ludvík Svoboda was a Czechoslovak general who commanded the Czechoslovak units raised in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/1st-czechoslovak-army-corps">1st Czechoslovak Army Corps</a>. Defence minister after 1945, he was purged in the 1950s and later rehabilitated. As president from 1968 to 1975 he resisted Soviet pressure during the 1968 invasion but remained in office under normalisation.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ludvik-svoboda.jpg" alt="Ludvík Svoboda" width="264" height="343" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Original photo taken by Stanislav Tereba, http://www.tereba.com/ The first derivated version by Fredy.00 This derivat... · CC BY-SA 3.0 cz · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ludv%C3%ADk_Svoboda_1968.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
